Implemented the REL-3 phase-neutral contract scope tuning. No commit made.

Changed:
- Added `PHASE_NEUTRAL_TOOLS` in [scopes.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/contract/scopes.py:58) and compile it into every phase with the active `ready_for_*_verification` finalizer alias.
- Kept mutation discipline phase-owned: `file_write` is still not allowed in EDIT, while `file_edit`/`file_replace_lines` remain allowed there.
- Updated guard wording and `_governed()` in [enforce.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/contract/enforce.py:50) so scoped tools include VERIFY now that finalizers are explicit neutral tools.
- Did not add unregistered static/app pseudo-tool names to the allowlist, so “permitted here” reasons stay precise.

Live audit distribution I saw from `/tmp/disco-agent.log`:
`edit shell=22`, `edit update_plan_progress=15`, `edit verify_web_app=10`, `edit browser=7`, `edit preview_start=6`, `edit file_write=4`, `edit code_exec=3`, `bootstrap update_plan_progress=3`.
The neutral denies are addressed; `shell`, `browser`, `code_exec`, and raw `file_write` remain non-neutral.

Existing scope expectation changes:
- `test_scopes_project_the_packs_per_phase`: exact phase sets now include neutral tools + active finalizer; `export` is neutral-only instead of empty because every phase permits neutral tools.
- Verify scope tests now expect `preview_start`/`preview_stop` as allowed neutral preview controls, not VERIFY mutators.
- Builtin contract scope checks now assert neutral/finalizer availability across every phase, while still asserting broad mutators stay out of VERIFY.

